.TH CAYMAN-TERMINAL 1 "September 2026" "cAIman Terminal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cayman-terminal \- native Bash terminal with a local assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cayman-terminal
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
cAIman Terminal combines independent Bash tabs with a compact assistant pane.
A local GGUF model provides assistance; known host errors and common command
options use installed documentation directly.
.PP
The assistant shows Ready.. after loading. Suggestions are never executed
automatically. Tab places a validated suggestion into the editable Bash input;
a separate Enter runs the command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-model " PATH
Load this local GGUF model. The development default is
artifacts/models/qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-sft-v2.gguf relative to the working directory.
The local installer creates a launcher with an absolute model path.
No model is downloaded automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-no-ai
Start a plain terminal without loading the model.
.TP
.BI "\-\-theme " ID
Override the saved theme for this window. This option does not change the saved
preference. Selecting a theme from the menu saves it for future windows.
.TP
.B \-\-list-themes
Print bundled theme IDs and exit.
.TP
.BI "\-\-ask " TEXT
Run a headless assistant request and print its validated JSON response.
Does not execute the suggested command. Cannot be combined with \-\-no-ai.
.TP
.BI "\-\-audit-report " PATH
Replay a saved JSON benchmark through static syntax and risk validation.
Does not infer, execute candidates, or verify remote executable availability.
Returns failure if a recorded critical candidate remains stageable.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print an ASCII caiman and a short usage summary, then exit.
.SH SETTINGS
Open Settings from the tab-bar menu or press Ctrl+,.
Appearance, assistant behavior, local model, inference limits and detected host
information are grouped in one window. Theme applies on Save; other preferences
apply after relaunching cAIman.
.PP
Model selection precedence is explicit \-\-model, saved model_path,
CAYMAN_DEFAULT_MODEL supplied by the launcher, then the bundled default (SFT v2).
Only registered model, terminal and shell providers are accepted.
.SH INTERACTION
At the normal Bash prompt, prefix a request with @ and press Enter:
.PP
.nf
  @ explain the error
  @ find log files larger than 500 MB
  @ continue
.fi
.PP
Requests beginning with @ are intercepted and do not execute as shell commands.
Each submitted request and its reply remain in that tab's scrollable AI pane
for the lifetime of the tab. Automatic hints update without erasing this conversation.
.PP
Pausing after eligible input requests assistance after approximately 250 ms;
model inference and documentation lookup add processing time.
.PP
A trailing dash or flag prefix, such as ps \- or ps \-\-so, shows options from
installed help or man pages. Bare find offers a simple file-search command.
Missing arguments receive guidance rather than invented values.
.PP
Failed foreground commands and completed assistant suggestions can trigger a
follow-up using recent command output and exit status. Interrupts and successful
unrelated commands normally stay quiet. Clearing the display retains context;
a new tab starts with fresh context.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+T
Create a tab.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+W
Close the current tab. A running foreground command must finish or be stopped first.
.TP
.B Shift+Left / Shift+Right
Switch tabs. Ctrl+PageUp / Ctrl+PageDown also work.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+A
Show or hide the assistant pane.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C / Ctrl+Shift+V
Copy or paste terminal text.
.TP
.B Tab
Stage a current suggestion. Otherwise use normal Bash completion.
.SH THEMES
The menu contains a Theme submenu. Changes apply immediately to all tabs in
that window, including terminal ANSI colors, cursor, selections, and assistant.
New tabs inherit the selected theme.
.PP
Bundled IDs: cayman (default), dracula, nord, gruvbox-dark,
catppuccin-mocha, and tokyo-night.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cayman-terminal/settings.json
Versioned appearance, assistant, model, inference and terminal preferences. Defaults to ~/.config/cayman-terminal/settings.json
when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset or not absolute.
.TP
.I /tmp/cayman-session-*/
Private per-tab Bash integration and event files, normally removed on exit.
A different temporary directory may be selected by TMPDIR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for saved preferences.
.TP
.B HOME
Fallback home directory for preferences and user Bash configuration.
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Optional location for temporary session files.
.SH LIMITATIONS
This preview supports local Bash with Emacs Readline bindings.
Direct SSH sessions pause local assistance; full remote integration, arbitrary
shell constructs, aliases, multiline input, and complete command semantics are
not supported by the validator. Man-page and flag coverage is bounded.
.PP
No cloud inference, telemetry service, or automatic model download is used.
The local model can be wrong. Inspect suggestions and their risk messages before
pressing Enter. A suggestion does not provide automatic undo.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates successful completion. Nonzero indicates a command-line,
headless inference, audit, or startup error. Missing model support in a desktop
window does not prevent the terminal from running.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
  cayman-terminal --theme nord
  cayman-terminal --no-ai
  cayman-terminal --model /path/to/model.gguf
  cayman-terminal --ask 'show disk space'
  cayman-terminal --list-themes
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR find (1),
.BR ps (1),
.BR man (1)
